<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Articles of Confederation</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1781–1789</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Articles of Confederation were the first constitution of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, adopted by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/continental-congress">Continental Congress</a> in 1777 and in force from 1781 to 1789. They created a loose league of sovereign states with a single-chamber Congress that could not levy taxes or regulate trade, weaknesses that led to the Constitutional Convention of 1787.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/articles-of-confederation.jpg" alt="Articles of Confederation" width="320" height="516" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The U.S. Government. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Articles_page1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
